        "subject": "LU-20739 build: check vfs_mkdir() and can_mmap_file() alone",
        "message": "LU-20739 build: check vfs_mkdir() and can_mmap_file() alone\n\nRHEL 10.3 (kernel 6.12.0-264) backports half of two upstream changes,\nand the client modules fail to build on it:\n\n- can_mmap_file() without vfs_mmap_prepare(), so the can_mmap_file()\n  that lustre_compat defines without HAVE_VFS_MMAP_PREPARE is a\n  redefinition.\n- inode_operations.mkdir returning a dentry without vfs_mkdir()\n  returning one, so ll_vfs_mkdir(), keyed on\n  HAVE_IOPS_MKDIR_RETURNS_DENTRY, assigns an int to a dentry in\n  pcc_mkdir().\n\nAdd HAVE_CAN_MMAP_FILE and HAVE_VFS_MKDIR_RETURNS_DENTRY and key the\ntwo compat helpers on them.  vfs_mkdir() with a delegate argument\nreturns a dentry as well but fails the new test, so the delegate test\ndefines HAVE_VFS_MKDIR_RETURNS_DENTRY too.\n\nAlso make the vfs_mmap() fallback use call_mmap().  On RHEL 10.3,\next4 sets only .mmap_prepare, which the kernel's can_mmap_file()\naccepts, so pcc_file_mmap() on an ext4 PCC backend would call a NULL\n.mmap.  RHEL 10.3's call_mmap() handles .mmap_prepare, and on older\nkernels it calls .mmap as before.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-pcc\nFixes: 323a6672b7c0 (\"LU-19137 build: Compatability updates for kernel v6.15\")\nFixes: e1c0eae673cc (\"LU-20388 pcc: fix PCC mmap due to deprecated mmap()\")\nSigned-off-by: Markus Hilger <markus.hilger@megware.com>\nChange-Id: I0f8c692bdc2deb0d351de51b9acc0b38faa91127\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
